<title>USA: U.S. Nov business inventories rose 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Nov business inventories rose 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commerce Department said U.S. November business inventories rose 0.1 percent after a 0.5 percent increase in October. It said November business sales rose 0.6 percent after a revised 0.4 percent increase in October.</p>
<p>The following lists business inventories and sales by sector, in billions of dollars, seasonally adjusted:</p>
<p>    INVENTORIES: November   October---Rev from  September</p>
<p>Total Business  1,011.96  1,011.26  1,011.35  1,006.43  Durable Goods     609.44    610.32    610.15    608.19</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  402.52    400.94    401.20    398.25</p>
<p>    INVENTORIES: November   October---Rev from  September</p>
<p> Manufacturers     439.89   438.13    437.91     436.70</p>
<p> Retailers	   314.05   315.36    314.83     312.77</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     87.86    89.60     89.97</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 258.02   257.77    258.61     256.96</p>
<p>    SALES:	 November   October---Rev from  September</p>
<p> Total Business    729.83   725.79    724.24     722.69</p>
<p> Durable Goods     360.75   357.53    356.50     358.37</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  369.08   368.26    367.74     364.33</p>
<p>    SALES:	 November   October---Rev from  September</p>
<p> Manufacturers     318.28   315.51    315.42     315.16</p>
<p> Retailers	   206.97   207.49    206.84     206.13</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     50.55    51.05     50.77</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 204.58   202.79    201.98     201.40</p>
<p> Inventory-To-   November   October---Rev from  September</p>
<p>  Sales Ratio	  1.39     1.39	1.40	 1.39</p>
<p>The inventory-to-sales ratio is a measure of how long it would take to sell existing stocks at the current pace.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected November business inventories to rise 0.3 percent.</p>
<p>The department revised October business sales from a previously reported 0.2 percent increase.</p>
<p>The rise in total business sales in November was the third straight monthly increase.</p>
<p>Retail inventories in November fell 0.4 percent, posting the first decline since they fell 0.9 percent in March 1996. Most of the decline came in the automotive and furniture sectors.</p>
